# Clover Mobile Rule

- Prefer strongly typed interfaces and avoid `any` unless unavoidable.
- Keep screen components focused on UI orchestration; move data logic into services/hooks.
- Reuse existing API wrappers and shared components before creating new patterns.
- Guard async calls with loading/error states and user-friendly fallback messaging.
- Preserve navigation and platform behavior conventions already used in Clover.

## Safety checks before finishing

- Verify affected screens compile and navigation flows still work.
- Confirm API/service changes remain backward compatible with current callers.
